  "verbalization": "Fluphenazine, a phenothiazine derivative, is linked to Calm2 through a series of molecular and pharmacological relationships. The evidence suggests that Fluphenazine, as part of the phenothiazine class, binds to Calm2 via a shared mechanism with Trifluoperazine, a closely related compound. This binding is supported by the lowest common ancestor (LCA) relationship between Fluphenazine and Trifluoperazine, which both belong to the broader category of antipsychotic agents. The LCA between Fluphenazine and Trifluoperazine further reinforces the pharmacological link, as both are classified under the antipsychotic agent category. The evidence also indicates that Fluphenazine resembles Clocapramine, a compound that binds to Calm2, suggesting a potential mechanism of action that is consistent across different members of the phenothiazine family. The integration of these relationships highlights a core pharmacological pathway where antipsychotic agents, through their shared structural and functional properties, interact with Calm2, potentially modulating its activity.",
